<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">webclient</ansi>

In the web client, the panels either side of the story show your world
and your company. Everything they show, a command shows too, and every
button in them just types a command for you.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The left column: the world</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Time and Date</ansi>, then the <ansi fg="yellow">Map</ansi>, then the <ansi fg="yellow">Room</ansi> you stand in (its exits
  and who's here), and the <ansi fg="yellow">Tutorial</ansi> while you're taking the course.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The right column: the dock</ansi>

  Always at the top: your health and mana, a line for each companion
  (health, and mana for one who casts; one not with you is dimmed; a
  fallen one shows how long is left to raise them), and one line of
  warnings when someone is hungry, thirsty, tired, cold, or the load is
  heavy.

  Below it, the tabs:

  <ansi fg="yellow">Character</ansi>   Overview (your sheet, experience, and gold), Gear (what you
              wear and carry, and its weight), Skills (with your jobs),
              Quests, Effects, and Pet when you have one.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Company</ansi>     Status (formation and each member), Inventory (everyone's
              gear, your horses, and the cargo), and Camp.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Combat</ansi>      Setup (how your company fights: formation, each member's
              role and target rule, and your company tactics), and the
              Battle view during a battle.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Comm</ansi>        what's said around you; a number on the tab counts what
              arrived while you were looking elsewhere.

  Turn on <ansi fg="yellow">Online</ansi> or <ansi fg="yellow">KillStats</ansi> in Settings and they join as <ansi fg="yellow">Who</ansi>
  and <ansi fg="yellow">Kills</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What the buttons and menus send</ansi>

  Inventory: click one of your items to look at it, put it in the cargo
  (<ansi fg="command">cargo put</ansi>), give it to a companion with you (<ansi fg="command">give</ansi>), or eat, drink,
  equip, or remove it; click a cargo stack to take one (<ansi fg="command">cargo take</ansi>,
  a partly used one first); click a horse
  to fit or take off a saddle, or release it (it asks first). Meal, Eat,
  and Drink feed everyone with you (<ansi fg="command">company meal</ansi>).

  Camp: Make camp, Light fire, Rest, Break camp, and Inn appear only
  when they would work (<ansi fg="command">camp</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">inn</ansi>); Meal is always there.

  Menus work from the keyboard too: Enter opens one, the arrow keys move,
  Enter chooses, and Escape closes it.

  Combat: click a member to change their role or target rule (<ansi fg="command">strategy</ansi>)
  or where they stand (<ansi fg="command">formation</ansi>). A guardian's menu picks whom it
  guards ("Guard: ..."), and its row says so, marked "(out of reach)" when
  it stands too far from its ward (<ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>); click Company tactics to set the
  focus or healing threshold (<ansi fg="command">company tactics</ansi>; the row appears once you
  have a company, and during a battle it only shows your saved tactics). Scout appears when
  enemies are here (<ansi fg="command">scout</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The Battle view</ansi>

  While you fight, the Combat tab shows the battle; when it ends, it goes
  back to Setup. If you're looking at another tab when a battle begins,
  a marker on the Combat tab tells you; it never switches tabs for you.

  The enemy group stands above, your company below (or just "You" when
  you fight alone), each front row nearest the middle, the way <ansi fg="command">scout</ansi>
  draws them. Your company shows its health as numbers; each enemy's
  health reads unhurt, scratched, wounded, badly wounded, or near death,
  never numbers, and a dot marks the ones you can reach from your place.
  In the dark you see only that it's too dark to make them out.
  Lines run from each fighter to whom it strikes; someone outside your
  company that an enemy strikes shows under "Also fighting". Point at a
  fighter, tab to it, or tap it to light it up with its target and
  everyone striking it.

  Below the grids: who has fallen ("Fallen"), the groups
  "Waiting their turn", and the same lines as a list
  ("Tamsin → the captain"). Click a companion to change their role,
  target rule, or place (the battle plays out by these); the full Setup
  is folded under the view. Flee tries to get away (<ansi fg="command">flee</ansi>).

  Above the grids, the Focus buttons call a new focus for this battle
  (<ansi fg="command">company tactics focus</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help tactics</ansi>): the current one is marked,
  and all of them wait, greyed out, until your company has turned at the
  next round. "saved" goes back to your saved focus.

  A guardian shows whom it guards and how many guards it has left under
  its name ("guards you, 1 guard left").

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Arranging it</ansi>

  The button at the top right of the dock opens the tab you're looking
  at in a window of its own; that window's dock button puts it back.
  Drag the dock's title bar to move it to the other side, and drag the
  column's edge to widen it. The client remembers your tabs and layout.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Settings > Reset Layout</ansi> puts everything back where it started.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company inventory</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help tactics</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help scout</ansi>.
